Pham et al. (2026 RF) “a small fraction of rounds in Pitchbook have no clear series information. For these cases, we approximate the series label of a round by first using available information from its lead or lag round (e.g., a round is assumed to be a Series B round if its previous round is already identified as a Series A), and then by the order of the round (e.g., the first round is Seed, the second round is Series A, etc.)&#x20;



DeSantola et al. (2023 OS) “Here, we measured the number of milestones passed based on the completion of VC rounds and/or an initial public offering. This variable ranged from zero to four. We coded each of the first three formal rounds of VC finance (series A, B, and C) as one, two, and three, respectively. Firms that had completed an initial public offering at time t were coded as four. Here, we build on prior work that analytically treats raising a round of VC financing and undertaking an IPO as incremental increases in development progress.  이 방식 참고해서 업데이트해줘. C:\Users\user\iCloudDrive\5학기\연구미팅\20240108-2010 to 2015 firms 폴더안 2010 2015 Crunchbase deals merged_v4 파일이야
